{# _main_base.cc.j2 — engine-agnostic heliaPROFILER firmware skeleton. #}
{#- Extracted from main.cc.j2 (#154 phase 4); main_aot.cc.j2 joined as a
   second child in step 3 and main_executorch.cc.j2 as the third in step 4.
   Everything outside an `engine_*` block is shared by every inference engine;
   the blocks are the only place engine-specific code may appear.  Keep it
   that way: a child template can override a block, but it can never remove
   base text.

   Whitespace contract -- the render env has trim_blocks=False and
   lstrip_blocks=False, so every newline around a tag is real output:

     * A region block's anchor is glued to the END of the preceding line and
       its content carries its own LEADING newline; this line's trailing
       newline terminates the block's last line.  Overriding a region with
       empty content therefore deletes the region cleanly.
     * A single-line block sits alone on the line it replaces and its content
       is one line with no newlines (indentation included where the site is
       used only once, supplied by the base where the same one-liner is
       reused at several indents -- see engine_invoke).
     * A THIRD shape, and the one with teeth: an anchor glued to the end of a
       `//` COMMENT line (engine_pass_preamble, engine_pass_warmup_arm,
       engine_pass_profile_arm).  The override's content MUST begin with its
       own newline -- content that does not is appended to the comment and is
       silently commented out of the firmware, with no render error and no
       compile error.  Enforced at source level by
       tests/contracts/test_template_blocks.py so it cannot regress quietly.

   Two deviations from the two clean shapes exist and are deliberate; they are
   written down here so the contract above is the whole truth:

     * engine_window_restore inverts the region convention -- heliaAOT's
       override glues its first line to the block tag and carries the TRAILING
       newline instead of the leading one, because the base anchors it to the
       END of an `if not power_only` opening tag that is itself at the start of
       a line, so there is no preceding text for the region's first line to be
       appended to.  Overriding it empty still deletes the region cleanly.
     * engine_iteration_setup's anchor is glued to a self.engine_reset_inputs()
       expansion rather than to a comment: its overrides lead with a newline
       for the same reason the comment-glued anchors must, but a mistake there
       merely joins two statements on one line instead of commenting one out.

   The measured window must not be timed by a clock this binary cannot read:
   DWT->CYCCNT dies with the CoreSight debug domain, which the dedicated
   power binary powers down or never holds up (measured ~7x wrong on Apollo4
   Blue Plus). Which clock times the window is resolved HOST-SIDE, once:
   the per-SoC half in SocCapabilities.power_window_timer, the per-render
   half (power_only, and the busy_loop probe's STIMER pin, issue #112) in
   firmware/context.py resolve_window_timer() -- read those docstrings for
   the full rationale. This template receives busy_loop_probe /
   window_timer / use_stimer_window as plain variables and carries no
   window-clock policy of its own (#118). #}{% block engine_file_header %}{% endblock %}

