{# pmu_profiler_sram_resident -- the per-layer instrumentation storage (heliaRT's
   g_profiler, heliaAOT's and ExecuTorch's g_layers) is SRAM-resident in every
   transport-attached render and left in default .bss in the dedicated power
   binary, where it is unused and an SSRAM power-on would perturb the very
   measurement that binary exists to keep clean.

   Set HERE, at the top, because TWO partials read it and one of them is the
   very next line: _system_includes.j2's narrow `#include "am_hal_pwrctrl.h"`
   guard folds this flag into its SRAM-residency test, and _ssram_power.j2
   (included ~160 lines below, next to main()'s SSRAM bring-up) folds it into
   the same test again.  Setting it down there instead left the include guard
   reading an undefined name -- StrictUndefined never fired because the guard
   spells it `pmu_profiler_sram_resident | default(false)`, so the disjunct was
   simply dead and the narrow header silently stopped being emitted.

   The SRAM-residency itself is a CHILD-declared fact (#161): every current
   engine keeps its per-layer storage SRAM-resident, so the block default is
   "true", but an engine that moves its array to TCM overrides
   engine_pmu_storage_sram_resident to "false" and its profile binary skips
   the unnecessary SSRAM power-on.  The block is declared inside a
   set-capture so it emits nothing; power stays an unconditional override
   here, not a child decision.  The vocabulary is exactly "true"/"false":
   anything else (a Python-spelled "True", a stray "1") hits the guarded
   empty-dict lookup below, whose KEY is the error message — StrictUndefined
   surfaces it verbatim, naming the seam, instead of a silently un-backed
   SSRAM array (#172 review, message wording round 2). #}{% set _pmu_storage_decl %}{% block engine_pmu_storage_sram_resident %}true{% endblock %}{% endset %}{% set _pmu_storage_value = _pmu_storage_decl | trim %}{% if _pmu_storage_value not in ("true", "false") %}{{ {}["engine_pmu_storage_sram_resident must render exactly 'true' or 'false', got '" ~ _pmu_storage_value ~ "'"] }}{% endif %}{% set pmu_profiler_sram_resident = (_pmu_storage_value == "true") and not (power_only | default(false)) %}{% include "_system_includes.j2" %}
