    // Lossless from boot: put the up-buffer in wait-for-space (blocking) mode
    // so HPX_READY and the entire HPX_START header are captured no matter when
    // the host attaches.  The firmware applies back-pressure (spins until the
    // host drains) instead of waiting on a host->target down-channel command.
    // That down-channel handshake is the fragile path that kept regressing
    // across SEGGER / SDK updates (stale D-cache on the down-buffer descriptor),
    // so we drop it entirely.  hpx_rtt_set_nonblocking() is restored before the
    // timed inference window so mid-inference heartbeats stay droppable and
    // never skew counts.
    hpx_rtt_set_blocking();
